--TEST--
An `initProperty` that leaves the property uninitialized makes the read throw a `LogicError`, and a class without `LateInit` throws on the first read — `rule:classes/late-init-initializes-on-the-first-read`, `rule:classes/an-unwritten-property-read-throws`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// covers: lang:classes/lateinit, LateInit
final class Post implements LateInit {
    public lateinit string $author;
    public lateinit string $title;

    public function initProperty(string $name): void {
        echo "init ", $name, "\n";
        if ($name == "title") {
            $this->title = "Hello";
        }
    }
}

final class Draft {
    public lateinit string $author;
}

Post $p = new Post();
try {
    echo $p->author, "\n";
} catch (LogicError $e) {
    echo $e->message, "\n";
}

// The property is still uninitialized, so the next read calls `initProperty` again.
try {
    echo $p->author, "\n";
} catch (LogicError $e) {
    echo $e->message, "\n";
}
echo $p->title, "\n";

// The same through `mixed`.
mixed $m = $p;
try {
    echo $m->author, "\n";
} catch (LogicError $e) {
    echo $e->message, "\n";
}

Draft $d = new Draft();
try {
    echo $d->author, "\n";
} catch (LogicError $e) {
    echo $e->message, "\n";
}
--EXPECT--
init author
`initProperty` returned, but `$author` is still not initialized.
init author
`initProperty` returned, but `$author` is still not initialized.
init title
Hello
init author
`initProperty` returned, but `$author` is still not initialized.
`Draft`'s property `$author` is read before it is initialized
